  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the tough-guy persona as the one making history",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the visual material of the man in the tough-guy persona (leather jacket, sunglasses, shotgun, cigar) who is portrayed as the one 'making history' in the context of the gay pride parade. This projection is achieved through the juxtaposition of the violent imagery with the celebratory text, suggesting the user (or the viewer) is identifying with or imagining themselves as the aggressive, dominant figure associated with the event. The meme's harmful intent relies on this projection to frame LGBTQ+ visibility as inherently dangerous or disruptive, which is a false and misleading interpretation.",
